    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0434" n="330" xml:id="pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4186: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-14T18:00:00+08:00">February 14, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 14—10:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50. Continuing my daily report number 45 of February 13, 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>1. In keeping with the day the situation[s] along both the Chapei and Woosung
                    fronts have remained comparatively quiet. Twelve thousand Japanese troops
                    reported to have landed at the N.Y.K. Wayside Wharf in the International
                    Settlement.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Legation, repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
